<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Marley returns for his first melanoma surveillance visit, about three and a half months after digit-sparing excision of a stage IA acral melanoma of the right great toe. The graft is fully healed, and he runs and plays football without pain; he still wears the ankle support for football since the sprain eight weeks ago, which has healed. He has examined his skin and nails each month with a mirror and photographed the graft; he has seen no change. His HIV, hepatitis B, and hepatitis C tests from the preventive visit were negative, with no immunity to hepatitis B, and he is due the second hepatitis B vaccine. He leaves on tour next week. He has had no thoughts of self-harm. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Graft</td><td>Healed; no change on his monthly photographs</td></tr><tr><td>Activity</td><td>Running and football without pain</td></tr><tr><td>Self-examination</td><td>Monthly, including the soles and nails</td></tr><tr><td>Results</td><td>HIV, hepatitis B surface antigen, and hepatitis C antibody negative; not immune to hepatitis B</td></tr><tr><td>Plans</td><td>Touring from next week</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

